2026-07-21 11:15:27,804 | INFO     | llm_service.py:177 | CTFs (Capture The Flags) and practice platforms are essential for ethical hackers to hone their skills. According to the primary evidence, some of the best resources for CTFs and practice include:

* Hack The Box (HTB) for open-ended realistic machines
* TryHackMe for guided beginner-friendly rooms and paths
* OverTheWire for classic Linux/security wargames
* PicoCTF for beginner-friendly, always-on CTF
* PortSwigger Web Security Academy for web security training
* HackTricks for a living cheat-sheet/reference book

These platforms provide hands-on experience and help build skills in areas like web security, networking, and penetration testing. They also offer a way to practice and apply theoretical knowledge in a real-world setting.

